(Bug #38: `exists` is not a file property - LANGUAGE.md documents the
idiom that answers "can this path be opened?" instead: open it inside an
`On error` handler. This exercises both branches of the idiom exactly as
written in the File Properties section.)

open a file for writing called setup at "/tmp/vox_test_exists_idiom.txt".
Write "hi" to setup.
Close setup.

open a file for reading called present at "/tmp/vox_test_exists_idiom.txt".
On error print "present: cannot be opened".
If present's descriptor is greater than -1 then,
    print "present: exists".
Close present.

open a file for reading called missing at "/tmp/vox_test_exists_idiom_missing.txt".
On error print "missing: cannot be opened".

Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_exists_idiom.txt".
